{"id":"mahabharata-4-030","work":"mahabharata","part":4,"partName":"विराटपर्व","partNameEn":"Virata Parva","unit":30,"title":"त्रिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 30 · Virata marches against the Trigartas","summary":{"en":"Hearing that the Trigartas have seized his cattle, Virata arms his army and his brothers, and has chariots and armour given to Kanka, Ballava, Tantipala and Granthika. The four disguised Pandavas ride out with the Matsya host.","kn":"ತ್ರಿಗರ್ತರು ಗೋವುಗಳನ್ನು ಹಿಡಿದಿರುವುದನ್ನು ಕೇಳಿ ವಿರಾಟನು ಸೈನ್ಯವನ್ನೂ ಸಹೋದರರನ್ನೂ ಸಜ್ಜುಗೊಳಿಸಿ ಕಂಕ, ಬಲ್ಲವ, ತಂತಿಪಾಲ, ಗ್ರಂಥಿಕರಿಗೂ ರಥ ಕವಚಗಳನ್ನು ಕೊಡಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ವೇಷಧಾರಿ ನಾಲ್ವರು ಪಾಂಡವರು ಮತ್ಸ್ಯಸೈನ್ಯದೊಂದಿಗೆ ಹೊರಡುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"त्रिगर्तों द्वारा गौएँ पकड़े जाने की बात सुनकर विराट अपनी सेना और भाइयों को सुसज्जित करते हैं, और कङ्क, बल्लव, तन्तिपाल और ग्रन्थिक को भी रथ और कवच दिलवाते हैं। वेशधारी चारों पाण्डव मत्स्य सेना के साथ निकल पड़ते हैं।","te":"త్రిగర్తులు గోవులను పట్టుకున్నారని విని విరాటుడు సైన్యాన్ని, సోదరులను సిద్ధం చేసి కంకుడు, బల్లవుడు, తంతిపాలుడు, గ్రంథికులకు కూడా రథాలు, కవచాలు ఇప్పిస్తాడు. వేషధారులైన నలుగురు పాండవులు మత్స్యసైన్యంతో బయలుదేరుతారు.","ta":"த்ரிகர்த்தர்கள் பசுக்களைக் கைப்பற்றியதைக் கேட்ட விராடன் தன் படையையும் சகோதரர்களையும் ஆயத்தப்படுத்தி, கங்கன், வல்லவன், தந்திபாலன், க்ரந்திகனுக்கும் தேர்களும் கவசங்களும் கொடுக்கச் செய்கிறான். வேடமிட்ட நான்கு பாண்டவர்களும் மத்ஸ்யப் படையுடன் புறப்படுகிறார்கள்.","ml":"ത്രിഗർത്തർ തന്റെ പശുക്കളെ പിടിച്ചെന്ന് കേട്ട വിരാടൻ സൈന്യത്തെയും സഹോദരന്മാരെയും ആയുധമണിയിക്കുന്നു. കങ്കന്, ബല്ലവന്, തന്തിപാലന്, ഗ്രന്ഥികന് എന്നിവർക്കും രഥവും കവചവും നൽകുന്നു. വേഷം മാറിയ നാല് പാണ്ഡവരും മത്സ്യസേനയോടൊപ്പം പുറപ്പെടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 4.30; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Dec  1 2011","sections":[{"title":"गोग्रहणपर्व","titleEn":"Gograhana Parva (The cattle raid)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततस्तेषां महाराज तत्रैवामिततेजसाम् ।\nछद्मलिङ्गप्रविष्टानां पाण्डवानां महात्मनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, the noble Pandavas of boundless splendor went on living in disguise in that finest of cities, and their time passed well as they did their work for King Virata."}},{"n":2,"text":"व्यतीतः समयः सम्यग्वसतां वै पुरोत्तमे ।\nकुर्वतां तस्य कर्माणि विराटस्य महीपतेः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus, Bharata, they spent their stay there, serving the king of Matsya, until the thirteenth year was ending."}},{"n":3,"text":"ततस्त्रयोदशस्यान्ते तस्य वर्षस्य भारत ।\nसुशर्मणा गृहीतं तु गोधनं तरसा बहु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Susharman, the king of the Trigartas, suddenly and forcefully seized a great many of Virata's cattle."}},{"n":4,"text":"ततो जवेन महता गोपाः पुरमथाव्रजत् ।\nअपश्यन्मत्स्यराजं च रथात्प्रस्कन्द्य कुण्डली ॥","meaning":{"en":"A cowherd wearing earrings rushed at speed to the city, leapt down from his chariot, and found the king of Matsya."}},{"n":5,"text":"शूरैः परिवृतं योधैः कुण्डलाङ्गदधारिभिः ।\nसद्भिश्च मन्त्रिभिः सार्धं पाण्डवैश्च नरर्षभैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king sat in his assembly hall, surrounded by brave warriors in earrings and armlets, by good counselors, and by the Pandavas, best of men."}},{"n":6,"text":"तं सभायां महाराजमासीनं राष्ट्रवर्धनम् ।\nसोऽब्रवीदुपसंगम्य विराटं प्रणतस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"That king, who made his realm prosper, sat in council; the cowherd approached him, bowed low, and said this to Virata."}},{"n":7,"text":"अस्मान्युधि विनिर्जित्य परिभूय सबान्धवान् ।\nगवां शतसहस्राणि त्रिगर्ताः कालयन्ति ते ।\nतान्परीप्स मनुष्येन्द्र मा नेशुः पशवस्तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The Trigartas have defeated us in battle, humiliated us and our kinsmen, and are driving off hundreds of thousands of cows. Rescue them, lord of men, so that your cattle are not lost.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"तच्छ्रुत्वा नृपतिः सेनां मत्स्यानां समयोजयत् ।\nरथनागाश्वकलिलां पत्तिध्वजसमाकुलाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, the king assembled the army of Matsya, thick with chariots, elephants and horses and crowded with foot soldiers and banners."}},{"n":9,"text":"राजानो राजपुत्राश्च तनुत्राण्यत्र भेजिरे ।\nभानुमन्ति विचित्राणि सूपसेव्यानि भागशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The kings and princes put on bright, variegated armor, splendid and well fitted, each taking his own share."}},{"n":10,"text":"सवज्रायसगर्भं तु कवचं तप्तकाञ्चनम् ।\nविराटस्य प्रियो भ्राता शतानीकोऽभ्यहारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Virata's beloved brother Shatanika took up a coat of mail of heated gold with a core of iron and diamond."}},{"n":11,"text":"सर्वपारसवं वर्म कल्याणपटलं दृढम् ।\nशतानीकादवरजो मदिराश्वोऽभ्यहारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shatanika's younger brother Madirashva took up a sturdy, well-made armor that covered him completely."}},{"n":12,"text":"शतसूर्यं शतावर्तं शतबिन्दु शताक्षिमत् ।\nअभेद्यकल्पं मत्स्यानां राजा कवचमाहरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king of Matsya himself took up a mail coat hardly to be pierced, with a hundred suns, a hundred spirals, a hundred dots and a hundred eyes."}},{"n":13,"text":"उत्सेधे यस्य पद्मानि शतं सौगन्धिकानि च ।\nसुवर्णपृष्ठं सूर्याभं सूर्यदत्तोऽभ्यहारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Suryadatta took up armor with a hundred lotuses and a hundred fragrant water lilies on its rise, gold on its back and bright as the sun."}},{"n":14,"text":"दृढमायसगर्भं तु श्वेतं वर्म शताक्षिमत् ।\nविराटस्य सुतो ज्येष्ठो वीरः शङ्खोऽभ्यहारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Virata's eldest son, the hero Shankha, took up a white coat of mail, strong with an iron core and marked with a hundred eyes."}},{"n":15,"text":"शतशश्च तनुत्राणि यथास्वानि महारथाः ।\nयोत्स्यमानाभ्यनह्यन्त देवरूपाः प्रहारिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hundreds of other great warriors, godlike in form and fierce in attack, armored themselves each in his own mail, ready to fight."}},{"n":16,"text":"सूपस्करेषु शुभ्रेषु महत्सु च महारथाः ।\nपृथक्काञ्चनसंनाहान्रथेष्वश्वानयोजयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great charioteers yoked horses, each to his own gold-armored chariot, in large, clean chariot-gear."}},{"n":17,"text":"सूर्यचन्द्रप्रतीकाशो रथे दिव्ये हिरण्मयः ।\nमहानुभावो मत्स्यस्य ध्वज उच्छिश्रिये तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the mighty banner of the king of Matsya, golden and shining like the sun and moon, was raised on his divine chariot."}},{"n":18,"text":"अथान्यान्विविधाकारान्ध्वजान्हेमविभूषितान् ।\nयथास्वं क्षत्रियाः शूरा रथेषु समयोजयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the brave Kshatriyas fixed their own various gold-adorned banners on their chariots, each as his own."}},{"n":19,"text":"अथ मत्स्योऽब्रवीद्राजा शतानीकं जघन्यजम् ।\nकङ्कबल्लवगोपाला दामग्रन्थिश्च वीर्यवान् ।\nयुध्येयुरिति मे बुद्धिर्वर्तते नात्र संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Virata spoke to his younger brother Shatanika: \"Kanka, Ballava, the cowherd and the mighty Damagranthi should fight too; I have no doubt of it."}},{"n":20,"text":"एतेषामपि दीयन्तां रथा ध्वजपताकिनः ।\nकवचानि विचित्राणि दृढानि च मृदूनि च ।\nप्रतिमुञ्चन्तु गात्रेषु दीयन्तामायुधानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Give these men chariots with banners and flags, and bright, strong yet supple armor. Let them put it on their bodies and be given weapons."}},{"n":21,"text":"वीराङ्गरूपाः पुरुषा नागराजकरोपमाः ।\nनेमे जातु न युध्येरन्निति मे धीयते मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"These men have the build of heroes and arms like the trunks of elephant kings; I believe they cannot fail to fight.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा तु नृपतेर्वाक्यं त्वरितमानसः ।\nशतानीकस्तु पार्थेभ्यो रथान्राजन्समादिशत् ।\nसहदेवाय राज्ञे च भीमाय नकुलाय च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the king's words, Shatanika hurried and ordered chariots for the Pandavas: for King Yudhishthira, for Bhima, for Nakula and for Sahadeva."}},{"n":23,"text":"तान्प्रहृष्टास्ततः सूता राजभक्तिपुरस्कृताः ।\nनिर्दिष्टान्नरदेवेन रथाञ्शीघ्रमयोजयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the charioteers, glad and eager to serve the king, quickly yoked the chariots as the king had directed."}},{"n":24,"text":"कवचानि विचित्राणि दृढानि च मृदूनि च ।\nविराटः प्रादिशद्यानि तेषामक्लिष्टकर्मणाम् ।\nतान्यामुच्य शरीरेषु दंशितास्ते परंतपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those tireless scorchers of enemies put on the bright, strong, supple armor that Virata gave them, and were fully armed."}},{"n":25,"text":"तरस्विनश्छन्नरूपाः सर्वे युद्धविशारदाः ।\nविराटमन्वयुः पश्चात्सहिताः कुरुपुंगवाः ।\nचत्वारो भ्रातरः शूराः पाण्डवाः सत्यविक्रमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fierce, disguised and skilled in war, all four of those Kuru bulls, the brave Pandava brothers of true valor, followed Virata together behind him."}},{"n":26,"text":"भीमाश्च मत्तमातङ्गाः प्रभिन्नकरटामुखाः ।\nक्षरन्त इव जीमूताः सुदन्ताः षष्टिहायनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Behind them came terrible rutting elephants, with temples streaming like rain clouds, fine tusked and sixty years old."}},{"n":27,"text":"स्वारूढा युद्धकुशलैः शिक्षितैर्हस्तिसादिभिः ।\nराजानमन्वयुः पश्चाच्चलन्त इव पर्वताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Trained elephant-riders skilled in battle rode them, and they followed the king like moving mountains."}},{"n":28,"text":"विशारदानां वश्यानां हृष्टानां चानुयायिनाम् ।\nअष्टौ रथसहस्राणि दश नागशतानि च ।\nषष्टिश्चाश्वसहस्राणि मत्स्यानामभिनिर्ययुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Eight thousand chariots, a thousand elephants and sixty thousand horses of Matsya marched out, led by skilled, obedient, cheerful men."}},{"n":29,"text":"तदनीकं विराटस्य शुशुभे भरतर्षभ ।\nसंप्रयातं महाराज निनीषन्तं गवां पदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That army of Virata shone, best of Bharatas, as it moved out, wishing to follow the cattle's trail."}},{"n":30,"text":"तद्बलाग्र्यं विराटस्य संप्रस्थितमशोभत ।\nदृढायुधजनाकीर्णं गजाश्वरथसंकुलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The finest force of Virata set out looking splendid, filled with men of strong weapons and crowded with elephants, horses and chariots."}}]}]}